+
+## Passkeys
+
+Sign-in, sign-up and account settings support passkeys (WebAuthn) via [SimpleWebAuthn](https://simplewebauthn.dev/):
+
+- **Sign up** with a passkey only (no password), or with a password and then an offer to create a passkey.
+- **Sign in** with the "Sign in with a passkey" button or straight from the username field's autofill (conditional UI). After a password sign-in, supporting browsers silently create a passkey (conditional create).
+- **Account settings** (`/account`) list your passkeys (provider name and icon, synced or device-only, created and last-used dates). You can create, rename and remove passkeys there.
+- **Reauthentication**: creating or removing a passkey requires a sign-in within the last 5 minutes. If it's older, you confirm with a passkey or your password.
+- The WebAuthn Signal API keeps passkey providers in sync: passkeys that were removed or don't exist get hidden, and the username shown in the provider stays current.
+
+Account and passkey records live in `.data/auth.json` (override with `AUTH_DATA_FILE`). The RP ID and expected origin come from the request URL. If you're behind a proxy, set them with `PASSKEY_RP_ID` and `PASSKEY_ORIGIN` (comma-separated).
